    "narrative": "For the Austin Waves on July 14, 2026, our offensive ceiling is heavily constrained by an unfortunate scheduling quirk that benches our core\u2014**Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** are all idle today, leaving us with a shallow pool of producers. Between our active roster, **Andy Pages** (42.71) serves as our strongest play, narrowly edging out **Drake Baldwin** (40.03). Both face a daunting challenge against Cease, whose 2.96 xERA dictates a significant regression in our baseline expectations. The lack of favorable platoon splits for **Andy Pages** and the reality of **Drake Baldwin** hitting in the bottom third of the order anchor both players near the \"marginal\" threshold, emphasizing a day of damage control rather than aggressive production.\n\nThe bench decision process today was largely academic given the number of players on off-days or the IL, specifically **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains sidelined. While **Andy Pages** captured the final active slot, the primary concern remains the high-skill profile of the opposing arm. We are essentially playing for accumulation rather than outcome, as neither **Andy Pages** nor **Drake Baldwin** possesses the elite sprint speed necessary to manufacture stolen bases in a tough matchup. We must rely on the park-adjusted xwOBA metrics for these two to navigate the efficiency floor; any deviation from the expected performance against the pitcher\u2019s strikeout stuff will likely result in an early benching to protect our remaining daily game caps for more favorable matchups later in the week.",
